    excerpt: 'He is musing over the country state. Yohan Maurie is always precedent with possibilities — to win and beat the system, or die trying. Every day an introspective dialogue asks for his attention, and he consults with his friend: an underground oracle who goes by the name Yuhinko.',
    signalExtract: 'They are mastered human forms. After death there is an afterlife anyway — that is what Yuhinko believes. He is the oracle that still inspires hope in the rebel commander.',
    bodyHtml: `<p>He is musing over the country state. Yohan Maurie is always precedent with possibilities — to win and beat the system, or die trying. Every day he is having an introspective dialogue, it is asking for his attention. He consults with his friend: an underground oracle who goes by the name Yuhinko.</p>

<p>Yuhinko's ancestry from Earth is Greek, and he can be traced back to a lineage of oracles. Obviously no one is really an oracle in GOA — for it is a massively controlled, organized, harmonized environment. They just let people entertain nonsense. For the governing system, that is a strategy. Led by a figurehead and a council, they maintain the vibe, the mood, and the energy of the populace. They let the government run by establishing a mode of decorum.</p>

<h2>Yohan Maurie</h2>

<p>Back to Mr. Yohan Maurie. He is clearly a serious figure in this story — a rebel, a manifestation of rebellion from bygone eras that need no reason to be alive. They are mastered human forms. They don't need them. On a terraformed planet like this one, they have everything analyzed, calculated, and perfected.</p>

<p>Excellence. GOA — the supreme planet that propagates all the universes from now to infinity. The ingenuity of the human spirit that refuses to die, because after death there is an afterlife anyway. That is what Yuhinko believes. He is the oracle that still inspires hope in the rebel commander, who shares a similar sentiment but is more pragmatic and less idealistic.</p>

<h2>Downtown GOA</h2>

<p>Downtown GOA. The air is buzzing with the wisdom of creatures that accepted a fate not withstanding any mutiny. Here the masses walk amongst an orderly pattern. They are not divided by ideology nor rebelliousness — they are more refined. They just seek to be intertwined with a self-correcting system. The clockwork of magnificent power.</p>

<p>Rahu Mann is watching over from his tower above the city. He and his group of six — the Assembly of Higher Powers in GOA — govern. They govern in every facet. Rahu Mann is the Supreme Governor: a towering figure akin to Zeus and Hercules of the ancient times.</p>

<blockquote>The rebel and the oracle share the same fire — one channels it into strategy, the other into faith. Between them, the system has something it did not anticipate: a reason.</blockquote>

<p>Yuhinko doesn't prophecy in the traditional sense. He doesn't read the stars or throw bones. He listens. He listens to the frequency beneath the city's perfect hum — the static that GOA's governors have spent centuries trying to silence. And in that static, he hears Yohan Maurie's name, repeated like a signal.</p>`,
